      "course_code": "CSCI-230",
      "title": "Computer Organization",
      "credits": 3.0,
      "description": "This is a three-hour lecture and two-hours lab each week. Emphasizes the fundamentals of computer organization and machine architecture, using a layered approach. Topics include data representation, the machine language execution cycle, microprogramming, addressing modes, and symbolic assembly level of language. Interconnection structures, memory, I/O, and fundamental notions of an operating system. Coordinated laboratory exercises allow students to experiment with program behavior and machine elements at each level.",
